window.__SLIDES&&window.__SLIDES('e2',{"s":["<section id=\"e2-tldr\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · 2019–2026</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Diverse partner pools, from FCP to generated partners</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px\">\n<div style=\"width:880px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Background · before the series</p><ul style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\"><li><b>Self-play breaks</b> · Self-play and PBT agents settle on private conventions and coordinate poorly with humans (Carroll et al. 2019).</li><li><b>Human-model recipe</b> · Carroll et al. cloned human play, then trained a best response to the clone; this needs costly human data.</li><li><b>Zero-shot coordination</b> · Other-Play (Hu et al.) needs known symmetries; OBL (guest) avoids conventions, and V2 reuses its Cat-Dog game.</li><li><b>Fictitious self-play</b> · It best-responds to past snapshots of itself; FCP borrows this idea for cooperative games.</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Problem</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Train an AI teammate in simulation that works with unseen partners, real humans included, in shared-reward Overcooked, ideally without human data.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Idea</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Train against diverse partners, then best-respond; later work aims the pool at gaps or generates partners online, and new benchmarks test the result.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<img src=\"assets/img/e2_tldr.webp\" alt=\"Lineage of the key papers in this work tree, drawn by year with arrows from parent to child\" style=\"width:736px;height:260px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">Backbone of the line. Arrows are inheritance, not baseline comparisons. White pills are guests: papers whose home is another tree, included because they sit on a lineage here.</p>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;background:#EFEBE0;border-radius:16px;padding:18px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Terms</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">ZSC</b> · teaming up with partners never met in training</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">Best response (BR)</b> · policy that does best against a fixed partner</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">Partner pool</b> · set of simulated teammates used for training</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">Human proxy</b> · behavior-cloned human model used as test partner</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Population training for humans</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">15 papers (1 guests) · 2019–2026 · FCP → MEP → GAMMA</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-assume\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · Assumptions</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Population training assumes shared reward and a simulator</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#801E1E\">Two players, one shared reward</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">All use two-cook Overcooked (OBL guest: Hanabi); E3T, ZSC-Eval add Football; V2 hides the recipe.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#801E1E\">Cheap simulation of partners</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Pools and best responses come from playing the game; V2 and OGC run in fast JAX versions of Overcooked.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#801E1E\">Little or no human data</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">FCP, MEP, HSP, E3T use none in training. Overcooked and Behavior prior need it; GAMMA-HA uses 20-50 games.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#801E1E\">Partners do not adapt</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Test humans are fixed policies (Overcooked, HSP); PECAN and E3T only read the partner&#x27;s recent moves.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#801E1E\">Known reward, fixed layouts</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">FCP names a known fixed reward as a limit; OGC varies layouts, V2 removes the full view.</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:center\"><div style=\"width:760px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Builds on</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3\">Self-play and PBT, Carroll et al.&#x27;s Overcooked human-model recipe, and the zero-shot coordination framing of Hu et al. (Other-Play, OBL).</p></div><svg width=\"48\" height=\"30\" viewBox=\"0 0 48 30\" style=\"flex:none;display:block;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0,9.0 L28.799999999999997,9.0 L28.799999999999997,0 L48.0,15.0 L28.799999999999997,30.0 L28.799999999999997,21.0 L0,21.0 Z\" fill=\"#801E1E\"/></svg><div style=\"width:816px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">So the series achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3\">Agents that beat baselines with real players (FCP, COLE journal, GAMMA, GOAT) and tests showing the problem is open (ZSC-Eval, V2, OGC).</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Population training for humans</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">15 papers (1 guests) · 2019–2026 · FCP → MEP → GAMMA</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-method\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · Evolution</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">From fixed partner pools to partners generated online</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:18px 32px\"><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.35\">A fixed pool misses partners, so each step targets the gap: hard partners, hidden preferences, then partners made on demand; benchmarks then test it.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px\">\n<img src=\"assets/img/e2_method.webp\" alt=\"Lineage of every paper in the work tree by year, arrows from parent to child\" style=\"width:1664px;height:560px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">Each arrow points from a paper to the paper that builds on it. Dark pills mark the key papers. White pills are guests: papers whose home is another tree, included because they sit on a lineage here.</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Population training for humans</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">15 papers (1 guests) · 2019–2026 · FCP → MEP → GAMMA</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-stages\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · Stages</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">The series unfolds in three stages</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:stretch\"><div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-top:8px solid #C8651B;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px\"><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:32px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.15;color:#C8651B\">1 · Human models, then pools</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">2019–2023</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">Overcooked</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">OBL</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">Behavior prior</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">FCP</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">MEP</p></div><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.35\">Overcooked best-responds to a cloned human; FCP: seeds plus checkpoints; MEP: entropy bonus, hard partners; OBL (guest): no shared conventions.</p></div><svg width=\"40\" height=\"28\" viewBox=\"0 0 40 28\" style=\"flex:none;display:block;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0,8.4 L24.0,8.4 L24.0,0 L40.0,14.0 L24.0,28.0 L24.0,19.599999999999998 L0,19.599999999999998 Z\" fill=\"#801E1E\"/></svg><div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-top:8px solid #3E6FD9;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px\"><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:32px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.15;color:#3E6FD9\">2 · Pools aimed at gaps</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">2023–2024</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">HSP</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">COLE</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">COLE (journal)</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">PECAN</p></div><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.35\">HSP: hidden-reward partners. COLE: hard-to-pair strategies from a game graph. PECAN: policy mixes plus a skill-level detector.</p></div><svg width=\"40\" height=\"28\" viewBox=\"0 0 40 28\" style=\"flex:none;display:block;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0,8.4 L24.0,8.4 L24.0,0 L40.0,14.0 L24.0,28.0 L24.0,19.599999999999998 L0,19.599999999999998 Z\" fill=\"#801E1E\"/></svg><div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-top:8px solid #8E4FC9;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px\"><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:32px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.15;color:#8E4FC9\">3 · Generate, then test</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">2023–2026</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">E3T</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">GAMMA</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">GOAT</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">ZSC-Eval</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">Overcooked V2</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7E3E3;border:2px solid #801E1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">OGC</p></div><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.35\">E3T mixes self with random; GAMMA samples a VAE; GOAT adds an adversary. ZSC-Eval builds test partners; V2 and OGC harden the game.</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Population training for humans</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">15 papers (1 guests) · 2019–2026 · FCP → MEP → GAMMA</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s01\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · Overcooked 2019 · 1 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Self-play agents coordinate poorly with humans</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Builds on self-play/PBT, PPO and behavior cloning (outside the tree). Sets the human-model recipe that Behavior prior keeps; V2 and OGC extend its environment.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Stationary human, shared reward</li><li>Some human-human data: 12-17 games per layout</li><li>One static agent per layout, trained offline</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked testbed; a behavior-cloned human model, then PPO trained against it (PPO-BC), annealing from self-play to the human model.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s01.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:338px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">Behavior prior keeps its recipe; V2 and OGC extend its environment; FCP, MEP, HSP and others only compare with it.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked, 5 layouts, 60 users: PPO-BC beats SP (p = .01) and PBT (p &lt; .01).</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">On the Utility of Learning about Humans for Human-AI Coordination</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Carroll et al. · NeurIPS 2019</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s02\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · OBL 2021 · 2 of 15 · Guest</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Guest OBL: plan as if the past were random play</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Home tree: Symmetry and belief. Builds on Other-Play, cognitive hierarchies and R2D2 (outside this tree); here only the source of V2&#x27;s Cat-Dog problem.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Turn-based cooperative game, partial view</li><li>Fixed starting policy pi0; learned belief model</li><li>Simulator to replay play from imagined states</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Reads past moves as played by a fixed pi0 (e.g. random) and plans the future as own pi1; iterating adds levels. Its Cat-Dog game needs grounded signals.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s02.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:62px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked V2 extends its Cat-Dog problem into layouts and expects OBL to do well there; V2 does not run OBL.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">2-player Hanabi (max 25), cross-play: level 4 scores 23.76 vs Other-play 21.77.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Off-Belief Learning</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Hu et al. · ICML 2021</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s03\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · FCP 2021 · 3 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Diverse self-play partners can replace human data</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Builds on fictitious self-play and Carroll et al.&#x27;s Overcooked (outside the tree); BCP is only a baseline, so FCP has no inheriting edge inside the tree.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Known, fixed shared reward; one task</li><li>No human data in training; zero-shot partners</li><li>32 seeds, picked and trained by hand</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Train 32 self-play agents, save 3 checkpoints each (start, 50% reward, end), then train one agent as a best response to the frozen pool.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s03.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:338px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">MEP, HSP, PECAN, GAMMA reuse its pool-then-best-response scheme or checkpoints; OGC builds its test pools the same way.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked, 114 humans: beats SP, PP, BCP (p &lt; 0.001); 10.6 vs 4.7 deliveries with human proxy (vs no checkpoints).</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Collaborating with Humans without Human Data</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Strouse et al. · NeurIPS 2021</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s04\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · Behavior prior 2022 · 4 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Start human models from optimal play, not random</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Keeps Carroll et al.&#x27;s human-model-then-best-response pipeline but initializes the human model from self-play weights instead of random weights.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Humans act closer to optimal than random</li><li>Human data from a few diverse layouts (40)</li><li>Tested only with a simulated human</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Copy a multi-layout self-play agent&#x27;s weights into the human model, then behavior-clone on little human data (OBP; OBP+f trains only the last layer).</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s04.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:108px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked-AI, simulated human: plain BC gets 0 reward; OBP gives working play from ~32k human steps.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Optimal Behavior Prior: Data-Efficient Human Models for Improved Human-AI Collaboration</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Yang et al. · NeurIPS 2022 HiLL Workshop (arXiv 2022)</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s05\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · PECAN 2023 · 5 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Mixed-policy partners plus a skill-level detector</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Uses MEP to build its population and FCP&#x27;s low/medium/high checkpoint levels; Overcooked agents are only baselines.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Two players, shared reward, no human data</li><li>Partners differ mainly by skill level</li><li>Level is readable from past play; frozen at test</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Train against random weighted mixes of population policies within a level group; a classifier infers the partner&#x27;s level and conditions the agent.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s05.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:200px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">E3T reuses its human-study interface code; no member builds on its method.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked, 15 players: 81.4% prefer PECAN over MEP; top score on all 5 layouts with a human proxy.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">PECAN: Leveraging Policy Ensemble for Context-Aware Zero-Shot Human-AI Coordination</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Lou et al. · AAMAS 2023</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s06\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · COLE 2023 · 6 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">COLE trains on the hardest-to-coordinate-with partners</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">No inheriting parent in the tree. Builds on empirical gamescapes, Shapley value and PageRank; FCP, MEP and Overcooked agents are only compared against.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Two-player common payoff; all pairs simulable</li><li>Population capped at 50; no real humans tested</li><li>Objective does not worsen across generations</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Strategies form a graph; weight partners by who others fail to pair with (Shapley value, PageRank); train a best response plus self-play (ratio 1:3).</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s06.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:246px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">The journal version extends it; E3T, ZSC-Eval and OGC only compare against or cite it.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked, 5 layouts: best with expert partners in 4 of 5 layouts (Table 1); best with human proxy in all 5.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Cooperative Open-ended Learning Framework for Zero-shot Coordination</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Li et al. · ICML 2023</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s07\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · MEP 2023 · 7 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">A max-entropy partner pool makes agents human-ready</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Same two-stage scheme as FCP, reusing its multi-checkpoint pool; also uses max-entropy RL and PFSP. Overcooked agents are baselines.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Two players, shared reward, no human data</li><li>Population close enough to the human policy</li><li>Entropy weight and priority strength set by hand</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">A population entropy bonus for 5 agents, then a best response that samples hard-to-cooperate partners more often over beginner/middle/best checkpoints.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s07.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:338px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">HSP, E3T, PECAN, GAMMA reuse its populations, objective or partner idea; OGC uses it to build test partners.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked: best of 6 methods on all 5 layouts with a human proxy; on par with human-human play (bar charts only).</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Maximum Entropy Population-Based Training for Zero-Shot Human-AI Coordination</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Zhao et al. · AAAI 2023</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s08\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · HSP 2023 · 8 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Prepare for biased humans with hidden-reward partners</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Follows FCP&#x27;s two-stage framework and puts MEP policies in half its pool; Overcooked is only the benchmark; TrajDiv is a baseline outside the tree.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Humans follow fixed policies for hidden event rewards</li><li>Rewards linear in game events, chosen by designers</li><li>Two players, full observability, 100M steps per policy</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Random hidden event-reward weights give biased partners; filter for diverse event counts; train an RNN agent on a pool of 36 (half MEP).</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s08.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:292px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">ZSC-Eval mirrors its event rewards and code; GAMMA and GOAT build their training code on its implementation.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked Distant Tomato, tomato-first script: reward 277.9 vs at most 23.3 for FCP, MEP, TrajDiv (Table 2).</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Learning Zero-Shot Cooperation with Humans, Assuming Humans Are Biased</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Yu et al. · ICLR 2023</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s09\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · E3T 2023 · 9 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">A noisy self-copy replaces the partner population</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Takes the skilled-and-diverse partner idea from MEP but drops the pre-trained population; reuses PECAN&#x27;s study interface; FCP is a baseline.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Two players, no human training data</li><li>Partner&#x27;s last 5 state-action pairs are visible</li><li>Randomness epsilon set by hand per layout</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Partner = (1 - eps) copy of the ego policy + eps random policy, trained end to end; a predictor guesses the partner&#x27;s next action from recent moves.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s09.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:292px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">No later member builds on it; ZSC-Eval only evaluates it (without partner modeling).</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked, human proxies: reward 114.1 vs MEP 89.7 (Table 2), at 1.9 h vs 17.9 h training.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">An Efficient End-to-End Training Approach for Zero-Shot Human-AI Coordination</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Yan et al. · NeurIPS 2023</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s10\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · COLE (journal) 2024 · 10 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">COLE makes each new AI partner one others prefer</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Journal extension of the ICML COLE: adds a human-AI setting, new theory and a second solver variant. FCP and MEP are only baselines.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Two-player shared reward; every pair simulable</li><li>New strategy reaches top-k preference centrality</li><li>Population capped at 50 for compute</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Same graph-and-Shapley/PageRank solver; adds COLE-R, a convergence result, an online human-AI platform and a 130-player study.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s10.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:292px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">ZSC-Eval reuses its human-experiment platform; no member builds on its method.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked, 130 players: preference for COLE-SV over baselines 0.68 to 0.88 (Table 4).</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Tackling Cooperative Incompatibility for Zero-Shot Human-AI Coordination</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Li et al. · JAIR 2024</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s11\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · GAMMA 2024 · 11 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Sample new partners from a VAE to train a Cooperator</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Layered on FCP and MEP populations (both), which supply the trajectories its VAE learns from; its code builds on HSP&#x27;s. PPO-BC (Overcooked) is a baseline.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Diverse joint-trajectory data exists</li><li>Humans fall inside what the VAE can generate</li><li>Two players; GAMMA-HA needs 20-50 human games</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">A VAE over partner trajectories; a fresh latent z each episode gives a new partner; one Cooperator trains with PPO; GAMMA-HA centres z on human games.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s11.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:292px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">GOAT freezes its VAE and lets an adversary pick latents.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked, 80 humans: GAMMA-HA 91.1 / 93.1 (Counter Circuit / Multi-strategy) vs best baseline 76.2 / 85.3.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Learning to Cooperate with Humans using Generative Agents</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Liang et al. · NeurIPS 2024</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s12\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · ZSC-Eval 2024 · 12 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">ZSC-Eval tests agents on diverse generated partners</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Partners mirror HSP&#x27;s event rewards and the code builds on HSP; the human platform is COLE journal&#x27;s. FCP, MEP, COLE, E3T are tested as baselines.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Deployment partners follow event rewards</li><li>Designers pick events and weight ranges</li><li>Partners and best responses trained in simulator</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Make partners with random event bonuses, pick a diverse set by best-response diversity (BR-Div), score agents by BR-Prox (return over best-response return).</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s12.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:292px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">No later member builds on it; OGC only cites it.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Rank match with humans: Spearman 0.90 (Coordination Ring) and 1.00 (Counter Circuit) over 5 algorithms.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">ZSC-Eval: An Evaluation Toolkit and Benchmark for Multi-agent Zero-shot Coordination</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Wang et al. · NeurIPS 2024</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s13\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · Overcooked V2 2025 · 13 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Overcooked hides too little to test coordination</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Redesigns Overcooked and extends OBL&#x27;s Cat-Dog game into layouts (both reuse). Trains FCP among 4 methods (comparison); Behavior prior, MEP, HSP only cited.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Two cooks, one shared reward; no humans tested</li><li>Partial view (radius 2), recipe hidden, no chat</li><li>Other-Play needs symmetries known in advance</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Shows the SP vs XP gap is partly state coverage; adds view radius, hidden recipe, random starts, signalling; Grounded layouts extend Cat-Dog.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s13.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:292px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked, 10 seeds: state-augmented agents&#x27; Counter Circuit XP 59 -&gt; 140; V2 gaps stay at 54-230.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">OvercookedV2: Rethinking Overcooked for Zero-Shot Coordination</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Gessler et al. · ICLR 2025</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s14\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · OGC 2025 · 14 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Training on generated layouts still fails on new ones</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Extends the Overcooked-AI benchmark and builds its test partners as FCP and MEP populations; UED methods PAIRED, PLR, ACCEL are outside the tree.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Two cooks, one shared reward, own view</li><li>Level generator in training; test layouts never seen</li><li>Layouts padded to one size; solvability unchecked</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">OvercookedUED: a layout generator and mutator; train with DR, PLR, ACCEL or PAIRED on generated layouts, test on hold-out layouts with unseen partners.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s14.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:292px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Hold-out layouts, 5 seeds: best agent (PAIRED + SoftMoE-LSTM) 13.1 vs oracle 216.8 mean return.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">The Overcooked Generalisation Challenge: Evaluating Cooperation with Novel Partners in Unknown Environments Using Unsupervised Environment Design</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Ruhdorfer et al. · TMLR 2025</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-s15\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · GOAT 2026 · 15 of 15</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">A frozen VAE keeps adversarial partners cooperative</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Reuses GAMMA&#x27;s partner VAE, frozen, and adapts HSP&#x27;s codebase; adds UED-style regret. FCP, MEP, BC+RL are baselines.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Simulated pool supplies VAE data (100k trajectories)</li><li>Enough data that the VAE does not overfit</li><li>Self-play score marks the achievable level</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">An adversary picks the latent code of the frozen VAE to maximize the Cooperator&#x27;s regret; the Cooperator trains to shrink it, so partners stay cooperative.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/e2_s15.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:246px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked, 40 humans: ~108 vs ~78 for GAMMA on Multi-strategy Counter (+38% per text); +3% on Counter Circuit.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Improving Human-AI Coordination through Online Adversarial Training and Generative Models</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Chaudhary et al. · ICLR 2026</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-eval\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · Evaluation</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Evidence moves from human proxies to harder tests</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:560px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-radius:16px;padding:22px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Benchmarks and baselines</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">Overcooked (5 layouts) dominates: score against a human proxy, held-out AI partners and online human studies.</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">ZSC-Eval, V2 and OGC change the test itself: generated partners, hidden recipes, unseen layouts.</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">Human studies range from 15 players (PECAN) to 130 (COLE journal); each paper picks its own baselines.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;background:#F7E3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:18px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Reading</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.35\">Benchmarks, partners and metrics differ: read each row alone as what that paper showed, not as a ranking.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-radius:16px;padding:20px 32px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472;padding-bottom:4px\">Headline result of each paper</p><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">Overcooked</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Overcooked, 60 users</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">PPO-BC beats SP (p = .01) and PBT (p &lt; .01)</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">FCP</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Overcooked, human proxy; 114 humans</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">10.6 vs 4.7 deliveries (no checkpoints); beats SP, PP, BCP</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">E3T</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Overcooked, human proxies</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">Reward 114.1 vs MEP 89.7; 1.9 h vs 17.9 h training</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">GAMMA</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Overcooked, 80 humans</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">91.1 / 93.1 vs best baseline 76.2 / 85.3</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">GOAT</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Multi-strategy Counter, 40 humans</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">~108 vs ~78 for GAMMA (+38% per text)</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">ZSC-Eval</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Overcooked rankings vs humans</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">Spearman 0.90 / 1.00 over 5 algorithms</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">Overcooked V2</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">V2 Test-Time Simple, 10 seeds</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">State-augmented self-play 161 vs cross-play -55</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#801E1E\">OGC</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Hold-out layouts, 5 seeds</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">PAIRED 13.1 vs oracle 216.8 mean return</p></div></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Population training for humans</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">15 papers (1 guests) · 2019–2026 · FCP → MEP → GAMMA</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"e2-open\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#801E1E\">Human populations · Open questions</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">What the series still leaves open</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:center;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-left:8px solid #801E1E;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 36px\"><p style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:64px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:#801E1E;width:56px\">1</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:32px;line-height:1.35\">Human results rest on proxies or small studies (15 to 130 people); some are bar charts only.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:center;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-left:8px solid #801E1E;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 36px\"><p style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:64px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:#801E1E;width:56px\">2</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:32px;line-height:1.35\">Designs need hand-set choices (HSP and ZSC-Eval event lists, E3T&#x27;s epsilon, MEP&#x27;s weights).</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:center;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-left:8px solid #801E1E;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 36px\"><p style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:64px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:#801E1E;width:56px\">3</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:32px;line-height:1.35\">Open gaps: V2 54-230, OGC 13.1 vs 216.8; V2 expects OBL to help on Cat-Dog layouts but never runs it.</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Population training for humans</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">15 papers (1 guests) · 2019–2026 · FCP → MEP → GAMMA</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>"],"n":["Members (15, chronological; 14 home members plus 1 guest): Overcooked 2019 (Carroll et al.); OBL 2021 (Hu et al., GUEST from tree &#x27;Symmetry and belief&#x27;); FCP 2021; Behavior prior 2022; PECAN 2023; COLE 2023; MEP 2023; HSP 2023; E3T 2023; COLE (journal) 2024; GAMMA 2024; ZSC-Eval 2024; Overcooked V2 2025; OGC 2025; GOAT 2026. Years as in the tree file (MEP circulated as a preprint in 2021). Inheritance edges (kind 0 builds on, 1 extends/reuses; 21 in all, the new one from the guest): OBL -&gt; Overcooked V2 (1, Cat-Dog problem extended into layouts); Overcooked -&gt; Behavior prior (0), Overcooked V2 (1), OGC (1); FCP -&gt; HSP (0), MEP (1), PECAN (1), GAMMA (1), OGC (1); MEP -&gt; E3T (0), HSP (1), PECAN (1), GAMMA (1), OGC (1); COLE -&gt; COLE journal (0); HSP -&gt; ZSC-Eval (0), GAMMA (1), GOAT (1); GAMMA -&gt; GOAT (1); PECAN -&gt; E3T (1, code of the study interface only); COLE journal -&gt; ZSC-Eval (1, human platform only). The other 38 edges are comparisons or citations (kind 2): every paper that lists FCP, MEP, Overcooked agents or COLE as baselines. COLE (ICML) has no inheriting parent; FCP has none inside the tree (its Overcooked edge is the BCP baseline). The figure keeps only the population backbone FCP, MEP, HSP, E3T, GAMMA, GOAT, ZSC-Eval; Overcooked, Behavior prior, PECAN, COLE, COLE journal, Overcooked V2 and OGC are left out for space, and so is the guest OBL: its only link is to V2, so it does not carry the line (a 9-node figure with OBL and V2 draws HSP-&gt;GOAT behind V2 and misleads). Shared problem: an AI trained in simulation must cooperate with partners it never met, including humans, in shared-reward games. Shared idea: diverse training partners plus a best response; the line moves from fixed pools (FCP, MEP) to targeted pools (HSP, COLE, PECAN) to partners generated during training (E3T, GAMMA, GOAT) and then to tests of the result (ZSC-Eval, V2, OGC). Background named in the notes: self-play and PBT; Carroll et al. 2019 human-model recipe; zero-shot coordination and Other-Play (Hu et al.); Fictitious Self-Play. Terms: ZSC, best response, partner pool, human proxy (behavior-cloned human model, used for testing). The fit of three members is by topic: Behavior prior needs human data and trains no population (it connects only to Overcooked); Overcooked V2 and OGC are environments or benchmarks, not training methods.","Assumptions shared across the line, with exceptions: (1) two players, one shared reward: all members; E3T and ZSC-Eval add Football 3v1 (3 agents); V2 adds partial views and a hidden recipe (two agents in all experiments, my reading). (2) Simulation access: partners and best responses are trained by playing the game (all members); V2 and OGC use fast JAX versions of Overcooked. (3) Human data: none in training for FCP, MEP, PECAN, HSP, E3T, COLE; needed by Overcooked (12-17 games per layout), Behavior prior (about 32k timesteps of a simulated human), GAMMA-HA (20 to 50 games). (4) Partner behavior: Overcooked models a stationary human; HSP assumes non-adaptive, consistent human policies; PECAN infers a skill level from past play, E3T predicts the next partner action from recent moves, both frozen at test time. (5) Reward and layouts: known shared reward (FCP states it as a limitation); five fixed layouts in most members; OGC varies layouts and V2 limits view radius to 2 cells. What the line grew out of: self-play/PBT, Carroll et al.&#x27;s human-model recipe, ZSC and Other-Play. What it reached: FCP beat SP, PP, BCP with 114 humans; COLE journal 130 players prefer COLE-SV (0.68 to 0.88); GAMMA 91.1 / 93.1 with 80 humans; GOAT +38% over GAMMA with 40 humans on Multi-strategy Counter (paper&#x27;s text); ZSC-Eval rank match with humans (Spearman 0.90 / 1.00); V2 and OGC show open gaps. Not assumed or not stated: observability is rarely discussed explicitly (MEP does not state it). Guest OBL (home: Symmetry and belief) assumes turn-based cooperative play (Hanabi), a fixed pi0 and a learned belief model; it is the one member outside the simultaneous-move Overcooked/Football setting.","Stage 1, human models then pools (2019-2023); OBL (2021, guest) sits here by date: it acts as if the past were a fixed pi0 to avoid conventions, and only V2 reuses its Cat-Dog game: Overcooked clones humans and trains PPO-BC; Behavior prior initializes the human model from self-play weights. FCP trains 32 self-play agents x 3 checkpoints, then a best response; MEP adds a population-entropy bonus and samples hard partners more. Stage 2, pools aimed at gaps: HSP gives partners random hidden event rewards (pool of 36, half MEP); COLE and its journal version find hard-to-pair strategies via a game graph, Shapley value and PageRank; PECAN mixes population policies and infers partner level. Stage 3, generate partners, then test: E3T (ego copy plus random mix, partner predictor); GAMMA (VAE of partner trajectories, new latent each episode); GOAT (adversary picks latents of the frozen GAMMA VAE to maximize regret). ZSC-Eval builds test partners with HSP-style event rewards and scores BR-Prox; OvercookedV2 hides information so partners must communicate; OGC trains on generated layouts and tests on hold-out layouts and unseen FCP/MEP partners. Edges relied on are the kind 0/1 edges listed on the first note. COLE (ICML) is placed by topic; the COLE line joins the rest only through ZSC-Eval&#x27;s platform reuse (kind 1) and comparisons. Edge for the guest: OBL -&gt; V2 is kind 1 (reuse of a problem design, inheritance not comparison). OBL has no comparison edges to this tree&#x27;s members.","Stage 1, human models then pools (2019-2023); OBL (2021, guest) sits here by date: it acts as if the past were a fixed pi0 to avoid conventions, and only V2 reuses its Cat-Dog game: Overcooked clones humans and trains PPO-BC; Behavior prior initializes the human model from self-play weights. FCP trains 32 self-play agents x 3 checkpoints, then a best response; MEP adds a population-entropy bonus and samples hard partners more. Stage 2, pools aimed at gaps: HSP gives partners random hidden event rewards (pool of 36, half MEP); COLE and its journal version find hard-to-pair strategies via a game graph, Shapley value and PageRank; PECAN mixes population policies and infers partner level. Stage 3, generate partners, then test: E3T (ego copy plus random mix, partner predictor); GAMMA (VAE of partner trajectories, new latent each episode); GOAT (adversary picks latents of the frozen GAMMA VAE to maximize regret). ZSC-Eval builds test partners with HSP-style event rewards and scores BR-Prox; OvercookedV2 hides information so partners must communicate; OGC trains on generated layouts and tests on hold-out layouts and unseen FCP/MEP partners. Edges relied on are the kind 0/1 edges listed on the first note. COLE (ICML) is placed by topic; the COLE line joins the rest only through ZSC-Eval&#x27;s platform reuse (kind 1) and comparisons. Edge for the guest: OBL -&gt; V2 is kind 1 (reuse of a problem design, inheritance not comparison). OBL has no comparison edges to this tree&#x27;s members.","Carroll et al., NeurIPS 2019 (p103). Edges used (tree e2): parent of Behavior prior (kind 0: keeps human-model-then-best-response, swaps random-init BC for optimal-behavior-prior init), Overcooked V2 (kind 1: V2 redesigns this environment) and OGC (kind 1: OGC extends the Overcooked-AI benchmark). Comparison only (kind 2): FCP (BCP baseline), MEP, COLE, PECAN, E3T, GAMMA, GOAT, HSP (layouts and human proxy models), COLE journal, ZSC-Eval (SP baseline). Numbers: user study 60 MTurk users, between-subjects (SP, PBT, PPO-BC), each plays 5 layouts; ANOVA F(2,224) = 6.49; PPO-BC vs SP p = .01, vs PBT p &lt; .01 (Sec. 6). With real humans PPO-BC is best in 3 of 5 layouts, on par in 2; effect weaker than in simulation (H-proxy). Reward per 400-step episode; 100 rollouts, 5 seeds in simulation. Each delivered soup gives both players 20. Assumptions: shared-reward multi-agent MDP; human modeled as stationary Markov policy (Discussion); 12-17 human-human games per layout (16, 17, 16, 12, 15 after filtering, Appendix A); static agent at test time; simplified kitchen (onions, dishes, soups; 6 actions; 5 hand-designed layouts). Caveats: bar heights in Figs. 4 and 6 are plots only (no values read). Main text says 18k timesteps while Appendix A implies about 36k per layout; I report only trajectory counts. Paper says it is the first analysis of the optimal-human assumption in deep RL. Code URL (HumanCompatibleAI/overcooked_ai) is from the abstract, not run.","Hu et al., ICML 2021 (p37). GUEST in this tree: home tree d1 &#x27;Symmetry and belief&#x27;. It sits here because of one inheritance edge: Overcooked V2 -&gt; OBL (kind 1; V2 temporally extends the toy Cat-Dog coordination problem of Hu et al. 2021a into its Grounded Coordination layouts). OBL has no other edge to a member of this tree: FCP, MEP, HSP, E3T, GAMMA, GOAT etc. do not build on it or compare against it. Idea: OBL acts optimally assuming past actions came from a fixed policy pi0 and future actions come from its own policy pi1; with a uniform random pi0 the policy is grounded (no arbitrary conventions); reusing pi1 as the next pi0 gives levels 2, 3, 4. LB-OBL learns a belief model of hidden state (in Hanabi, the own hand) and replays play from sampled states. Numbers, Table 1 (2-player Hanabi, max 25, 5 seeds, 5,000 games per model): cross-play OBL level 1 20.85, level 2 23.24, level 3 23.68, level 4 23.76; Other-play 21.77; K-Level 17.17. Self-play: OBL level 1 20.92, level 4 24.10, Other-play 24.14. With Clone Bot (human data): OBL 13.80 to 16.02 vs Other-play 8.55, K-Level 13.03. Toy Cat-Dog game: OBL level 1 earns +5 in every pairing; self-play agents earn +10 or -10. These are Hanabi numbers; they are not comparable to Overcooked results in this tree. Caveats: V2 only EXPECTS OBL to do well on Grounded Coordination (button indicator) and to struggle on Test-Time Protocol Formation; its experiments do not include OBL, and its Future Work says OBL &#x27;might offer improvements in some scenarios&#x27;. OBL needs turn-based play and a belief model, unlike the simultaneous-move Overcooked members. Code not checked.","Strouse et al., NeurIPS 2021 (p61). Edges used: Overcooked is only a comparison (kind 2, BCP baseline). Parent of HSP (kind 0: follows the FCP two-stage framework), MEP (kind 1: same scheme, reuses checkpoints), PECAN (kind 1: checkpoint skill levels), GAMMA (kind 1: FCP populations as the VAE&#x27;s data), OGC (kind 1: FCP populations as test partners). Comparison only (kind 2): COLE, COLE journal, E3T, ZSC-Eval, GOAT, Overcooked V2 (FCP is one of four methods trained in V2); Behavior prior cites it only as the claim that human data may be unnecessary. Numbers, Table 1 (5 seeds, mean deliveries over 5 layouts, 540-step episodes), FCP / FCP-T: human proxy 10.6 +/- 0.5 / 4.7 +/- 0.4; diverse SP 11.2 / 6.9; random partners 8.6 / 1.0. Table 2: N = 4 to 128 gives 8.4, 9.1, 10.2, 10.6, 10.4, 10.8 deliveries, plateau near 32. Human study: 114 Prolific participants, p &lt; 0.001 vs SP, PP, BCP (t = 12.3, 8.2, 7.8); preference for FCP p &lt; 0.05 vs every baseline. SP/PP/BCP bar values appear only in Figs. 5 and 7a, so none are quoted. Limitations named by the paper: known fixed reward, manual partner selection (researcher bias), maybe unrealistically large populations for harder games. 32 x 3 = 96 partners is my arithmetic.","Yang, Carroll, Dragan, NeurIPS 2022 HiLL workshop (p62). Edges used: child of Overcooked (kind 0). It cites FCP only to argue that human data is still needed for suboptimal human behavior (kind 2). Nothing in the tree builds on it (V2 and OGC cite it only as an example of work on few fixed layouts). Numbers: plain multi-layout BC from the 26x7x5 state gets 0 reward on all 5 test layouts (Sec. 6.1, Fig. 4). Validation loss averages (Table 3): BC 1.60, OBP 1.70, OBP+f 1.61; the paper calls loss inconclusive (plain BC over-predicts the wait action). Human data: simulated human H paired with itself on 40 layouts, ~32k timesteps (App. C.2), wait probability 0.5. Collaboration (Fig. 5): OBP-based best responses reach the highest reward with H on almost all layouts, sometimes narrowly; SP is superhuman and never waits. Caveats: only a simulated human, no real people (author-stated); reward bars in Figs. 4 and 5 have no printed values; my by-eye reading (OBP near H on layout e0, about 85 vs 93) is not used on slides. Venue is the NeurIPS 2022 HiLL workshop per the PDF. Network is 3 conv plus 3 FC layers, shared by human model and agents so weights can be copied.","Lou et al., AAMAS 2023 (p48). Edges used: child of MEP (kind 1: population built with MEP), FCP (kind 1: skill levels from checkpoints), Overcooked (kind 2: SP/PBT baselines). Parent of E3T (kind 1, code only: E3T uses PECAN&#x27;s human-AI interaction interface for its study). TrajeDi is a baseline outside this tree. Cited (kind 2) by COLE journal, GAMMA, ZSC-Eval. Numbers: Fig. 6b (15 players): preference PECAN 81.4% vs MEP 18.6%; adaptiveness 61.4% vs 38.6%. Table 1 (Asymmetric Advantages, with a human): dishes served 12.25 vs 6.75 (column header missing in extracted text; read as dishes served). Ablation: dropping the ensemble costs 18.1, dropping the context encoder 14.4 (reference point not stated; read as drop vs full PECAN). Human-proxy results: SP, PBT, FCP, TrajeDi numbers are taken from the MEP paper; PECAN and MEP run with 4 seeds. Method: partner = random convex mix of policies in one level group; group chosen by rank-based priority (worst ego performance favored); encoder (self-attention + MLP) predicts low/medium/high from past trajectories; two-stage, no test-time updates (end-to-end is future work). Caveats: Fig. 6a has no printed values; the Yang et al. (EPPO) build-on is my reading; Overcooked only; 15 players is a small sample.","Li et al., ICML 2023 (p50). Edges used: parent of COLE journal (kind 0). As child: only comparison edges (kind 2) to FCP, MEP, Overcooked (reimplemented FCP, MEP original code, SP/PBT from Carroll et al.). Comparison/citation only for ZSC-Eval (implemented as a ZSC algorithm), E3T and GAMMA (related work), OGC (listed). Numbers, Table 1 (expert partners, mean episode reward), COLE_SV 1:3 vs PBT per layout: Cramped Room 212.80 vs 209.83; Asymmetric Adv. 178.80 vs 161.50 (MEP 179.83 is 1.03 higher, the 0:4 row reaches 182.80); Coordination Ring 166.32 vs 158.83; Forced Coordination 86.40 vs 70.33; Counter Circuit 105.84 vs 64.00 (MEP 76.67). The 150.0 vs 132.9 average on the slide is MY average of those rows; the paper does not report it and layouts have very different scales, so it is not a headline. Method: Preference GFG graph, preference centrality, objective J(s, phi) = E_phi w(s, p) + alpha w(s, s) with alpha = 1; COLE_SV uses inverse weighted PageRank (damping 0.85) inside a Monte Carlo Shapley value; SUCG sampling; PPO oracle; up to 50 strategies, 60-80 generations per layout, 1-2 days per layout on a 2-GPU machine. Caveats: Fig. 5 (human proxy) values not readable; no seeds or significance for Table 1; proofs not checked; &#x27;no real humans tested&#x27; is my reading of the setup.","Zhao et al., AAAI 2023 (p63; PDF is an arXiv v3 preprint, venue from file metadata). Edges used: child of FCP (kind 1), Overcooked (kind 2 baselines). Parent of HSP (kind 1: half the pool is MEP), E3T (kind 0: splits its objective into ego plus random), PECAN (kind 1), GAMMA (kind 1), OGC (kind 1: MEP populations as test partners). Baseline (kind 2) for COLE, COLE journal, GOAT, ZSC-Eval. TrajeDi is a baseline outside this tree. Numbers: results are bar charts only (Figs. 4a, 4b, 5); no values quoted. Table 1 (Counter Circuit population entropy): alpha 0 -&gt; 0.988, 0.01 -&gt; 1.151, 0.04 -&gt; 1.791. Hyperparameters: population 5 (FCP uses 10 in the main comparison), alpha 0.01 (0.04 for Forced Coordination), beta 3, 1.1e7 steps per agent. Real-human test on Amazon Mechanical Turk (participant count not found); SP and PBT results reused from Carroll et al. Method: reward r - alpha log of the population&#x27;s mean policy; Theorem 1 says population diversity &gt;= population entropy (cheaper, bounded); partner i sampled in proportion to 1 / expected return with it (rank-based variant); Corollary 1 gives a human-AI bound if some population agent is eps-close to the human. Caveats: no observability assumption stated; I did not see an empirical check that the population covers human behavior; Appendix F.4.3 of HSP says MEP beats HSP in Coordination Ring with humans.","Yu et al., ICLR 2023 (p64). Edges used: child of FCP (kind 0), MEP (kind 1), Overcooked (kind 2: layouts and the Carroll human proxy models, not method). Parent of ZSC-Eval (kind 0: behavior-preferring rewards, codebase), GAMMA (kind 1: Cooperator training built on HSP code), GOAT (kind 1: codebase adapted from HSP and GAMMA). Cited only (kind 2) by COLE journal (its FCP-fails-with-tomato-player example), Overcooked V2, OGC. Numbers: Table 2 (Distant Tomato, tomato placement script, 5 seeds): FCP 15.6, MEP 20.1, TrajDiv 23.3, HSP 277.9. The text says about 10x; my arithmetic gives 12x to 18x. HSP is not best in every row (Many Orders, Tomato Place and Delivery: FCP 329.1, MEP 328.1 vs HSP 324.5). Table 4 (Many Orders, humans): reward FCP 316.81, MEP 320.61, TrajDiv 323.52, HSP 382.52. Human study: 60 volunteers (about 12 per layout). Learned human models (Table 1): HSP 300.3 in Asymmetric Advantages; comparable to MEP in Coordination Ring and Counter Circuit; paper calls the gain marginal there. Caveats: the 277.9 result is against a script the authors wrote; Appendix F.4.3 says humans rank MEP above HSP in Coordination Ring; no significance tests checked; compute-heavy (pool of 36, 5 seeds).","Yan et al., NeurIPS 2023 (p65). Edges used: child of MEP (kind 0: objective split into ego plus random), PECAN (kind 1: uses PECAN&#x27;s code for its human-AI interaction interface, study tooling only), FCP and Overcooked (kind 2 baselines), COLE and COLE journal (kind 2: related work). Parent of nothing with inheritance; ZSC-Eval implements it without partner modeling (kind 2); OGC cites it (kind 2). Numbers, Table 2 (average over 5 layouts, human proxies, 5 seeds; training time for one model on Cramped Room): SP 0.5 h / 65.8, PBT 2.7 h / 66.8, FCP 7.6 h / 71.7, MEP 17.9 h / 89.7 +/- 7.1, E3T 1.9 h / 114.1 +/- 6.4. 10.6% = 1.9 / 17.9. Real humans: 20 people, 600 rounds, E3T highest in a bar chart (Fig. 4b), no numbers. Football 3v1 (Table 3): zero-shot win rate 0.49 vs 0.07 for self-play. Epsilon: 0.5 in most layouts, 0.0 in Forced Coordination; accuracy of partner prediction about 55% at eps 0.5. Method: Eq. 4 partner = eps random + (1 - eps) ego copy; Propositions 1-3 bound entropy and the loss of best response; asymmetric input breaks conventions. Caveats: Fig. 1 compares against AI baselines, the 114.1 vs 89.7 numbers are against human proxies (not mixed); GPU named only for MEP (over 15 h); proofs not checked; test-time observability of partner actions with real humans not spelled out.","Li et al., JAIR 2024 (p51; venue from the file name, the PDF does not print it). Edges used: child of COLE ICML (kind 0). Comparison/citation only (kind 2): FCP, MEP (baselines), Overcooked (environment), PECAN (cited for human-preference studies), HSP (borrowed motivating example). Parent of ZSC-Eval (kind 1: COLE-Platform reused for human experiments). Numbers, Table 4 (130 valid of 148 students, one university, 10 games each against COLE-SV and one random baseline): preference vs SP / PBT / FCP / MEP = 0.88 / 0.70 / 0.85 / 0.68; fluency 0.87 / 0.71 / 0.78 / 0.60; understanding 0.80 / 0.63 / 0.78 / 0.61. Table 3 (COLE-SV vs COLE-R, human proxy): Coordination Ring 128.80 vs 98.40, Forced Coordination 46.40 vs 24.40, Counter Circuit 82.00 vs 57.60 (paper: about 30%, 91%, 43%). Table 2 (expert partners) repeats the ICML numbers. On Coordination Ring COLE-SV is slightly below MEP in the human study, attributed to MEP&#x27;s fixed route. Uncertain: which of COLE-SV and COLE-R is the &#x27;extra&#x27; algorithm is not stated; Table 2 column meaning is ambiguous; Figs. 9 and 11 are bars only; proofs not checked; the text refers to Table 1 where Table 4 is meant.","Liang et al., NeurIPS 2024 (p68). Edges used: child of FCP, MEP (kind 1, each used as the data source for the generative model), HSP (kind 1: the Cooperator&#x27;s PPO training is based on HSP&#x27;s implementation), Overcooked (kind 2, PPO-BC baseline), COLE and PECAN (kind 2, related work). CoMeDi, a third data source, is a paper outside this tree. Parent of GOAT (kind 1: frozen VAE as partner space). Numbers, Table 3 (80 Prolific users, 60-second games, Counter Circuit / Multi-strategy Counter): FCP 26.24 / 34.35; FCP+GAMMA 57.87 / 65.36; CoMeDi 56.87 / 27.11; CoMeDi+GAMMA 72.17 / 34.72; MEP 76.19 / 64.02; MEP+GAMMA 81.10 / 88.30; PPO+BC 53.51 / 85.26; PPO+BC+GAMMA 59.67 / 77.53; GAMMA-HA (MEP population plus human data) 91.11 / 93.09. GAMMA beats its own baseline in 7 of 8 pairs (my tally); PPO+BC+GAMMA is lower on Multi-strategy. Not significant: MEP+GAMMA vs MEP on Counter Circuit (p = 0.639), PPO+BC+GAMMA vs PPO+BC (p = 0.0748), GAMMA-HA vs PPO+BC on Multi-strategy (p = 0.426). Uncertain: text says GAMMA-HA surpasses the best baselines by 60% / 43%, Table 3 gives about +20% / +9%; I used the table. Which fine-tuning variant (DFT) the main GAMMA-HA row uses is unclear; text says 8 rounds but 9 policies. Limitation: CoMeDi data had no tomato soup, so CoMeDi+GAMMA also failed on tomato.","Wang et al., NeurIPS 2024 Datasets and Benchmarks (p111). Edges used: child of HSP (kind 0), COLE journal (kind 1: human experiment platform built on COLE-Platform); FCP, MEP, COLE, E3T, Overcooked (kind 2: algorithms evaluated, SP baseline); PECAN (kind 2: listed among methods using human proxies). It is an evaluation toolkit, not a training method. TrajeDi is an algorithm outside this tree. Numbers, Table 2 (Spearman between human and evaluator rankings, HSP/MEP/FCP/COLE/SP): Coordination Ring ZSC-Eval 0.90, human proxy 0.90, trained SP agents 0.70; Counter Circuit 1.00, 0.60, 0.10. Table 3 (Football BR-Prox, 95% CI): SP 0.20, E3T 0.66, FCP 0.78, MEP 0.78, TrajeDi 0.81, COLE 0.75, HSP 0.80. Human study: 152 recruited, 145 valid, 7 agents ranked on 2 layouts. Findings: old layouts (Forced Coordination, Asymmetric Advantages) barely separate algorithms; all algorithms score lower with expert partners. Uncertain: Spearman values come from only 2 layouts and 5 algorithms (coarse); on Coordination Ring ZSC-Eval only ties human proxies; main text says 9 Overcooked layouts, Appendix D.5 mentions 7; per-algorithm Overcooked BR-Prox only in plots.","Gessler et al., ICLR 2025 (p113). Edges used: child of Overcooked (kind 1: environment redesign; V2 is in JaxMARL) and of OBL (kind 1, guest from tree &#x27;Symmetry and belief&#x27;: the Grounded Coordination layouts temporally extend OBL&#x27;s Cat-Dog problem; the paper only expects OBL to perform well there and does not run it). Comparison/citation only (kind 2): FCP (trained and evaluated as one of 4 methods in V2), Behavior prior, MEP, HSP (cited as users of Overcooked and as cases where training is hard). Numbers (Tables 1-2, 10 PPO seeds, 500 episodes, mean over cross-play pairings). Table 1 standard SP / XP / gap -&gt; state-augmented SP / XP / gap: Cramped Room 259/257/2 -&gt; 259/255/4; Asymmetric Advantages 278/278/0 -&gt; 277/276/1; Coordination Ring 214/96/118 -&gt; 269/198/71; Forced Coordination 199/138/61 -&gt; 200/193/8; Counter Circuit 163/59/104 -&gt; 184/140/44. Table 2 (V2, state-augmented SP / XP / gap): Grounded Simple 156/-17/176; Grounded Ring 165/-16/183; Test-Time Simple 161/-55/230; Test-Time Wide 137/-12/142; Demo Cook Simple 170/112/54; Demo Cook Wide 192/60/138. Self-play XP in V2 ranges from -81 to 40; Other-Play improves XP in most layouts but stays far below SP; FCP has the lowest SP (22 to 95) and small positive XP (1 to 46). Setup: partial view radius 2; recipe sampled per episode and visible only at an indicator block; random start positions; communication through items and movement or a costly button; new network (1x1 convs, GRU). Caveats: the Gap column does not always equal SP minus XP (Test-Time Simple 161 - (-55) = 216 vs 230 in the table); I quote the table. Whether every V2 experiment is strictly two-agent is my reading. No human experiments. It is an environment paper: no new training method. FCP uses a population of 8 SP agents x 3 checkpoints here and is not tuned.","Ruhdorfer et al., TMLR 2025 (p115). Edges used: child of Overcooked (kind 1: extends the Overcooked-AI benchmark and JaxMARL&#x27;s Overcooked), FCP and MEP (kind 1: trains 24-agent FCP and MEP populations, low/mid/high skill checkpoints, as ad-hoc test partners). Citation only (kind 2): COLE, Behavior prior, HSP (cited; its CNN-LSTM policy follows prior Overcooked work), E3T, ZSC-Eval. Numbers (Table 1, SoftMoE-LSTM, mean episode reward over test layouts, 5 seeds, 95% CI): DR 4.21 +- 9.52, PLR 0.68 +- 0.75, PAIRED 13.12 +- 11.46, ACCEL 0.61 +- 0.55, Oracle 216.76 +- 34.41. Other networks: CNN-LSTM DR 2.84, PLR 0.18, PAIRED 0.52, ACCEL 0.24, Oracle 204.44; CNN-S5 DR 0.06, PLR 0.13, PAIRED 0.02, ACCEL 0.06, Oracle 166.63. Solved rate (at least two soups, appendix Table 12): DR 3.78%, PLR 3.68%, Pop. PAIRED 14.72%, ACCEL 0.04%, Oracle 99.7%. Setup: MAPPO; training on generated layouts; evaluation in self-play on the 5 original layouts plus transformed layouts, against FCP and MEP populations (24 agents each) and other seeds of the same method. Caveats: benchmark paper, no new algorithm; text says PAIRED solved rate 14.6 +- 7.7 vs 14.72 +- 12.2 in Table 12; text says 32 transformed layouts, Fig. 4 caption says 28; ad hoc results are bar charts only. No human partners.","Chaudhary et al., ICLR 2026 (p71; venue from the file name, the PDF is arXiv v4). Edges used: child of GAMMA (kind 1: frozen VAE), HSP (kind 1: codebase adapted from HSP and GAMMA), Overcooked, FCP, MEP (kind 2 baselines). CoMeDi is a baseline outside this tree. Nothing builds on it. Numbers: only +38% (Multi-strategy Counter) and +3% (Counter Circuit) are stated in the text (RQ3). Bar heights read from Fig. 4f, approximate (+/-2): BC+RL ~75, FCP ~36, CoMeDi ~13, MEP ~67, GAMMA ~78, GOAT ~108. Study: 40 Prolific players, 6 rounds, a different agent per round. Simulation against a behavior-cloned proxy: GOAT significantly higher than all 4 baselines in both layouts (values not read). Cost about a day per Cooperator, 24-36 GPU hours. Method: minimax objective incentivizes sabotage (Eq. 1); adversary maps z to z&#x27; for the frozen decoder; regret = partner&#x27;s self-play value minus cross-play value with the Cooperator (Eq. 4); adversary trained with REINFORCE and a KL penalty; Cooperator with PPO. Uncertain: &#x27;humans look like generated partners&#x27; is my reading of the motivation, not an explicit assumption; the algorithm box says the Cooperator &#x27;minimizes regret&#x27; while the text says it maximizes cooperation performance.","Milestone numbers (each from the member&#x27;s own notes; not comparable across rows): Overcooked: 60 MTurk users, ANOVA F(2,224) = 6.49, PPO-BC vs SP p = .01, vs PBT p &lt; .01. FCP: Table 1 human proxy 10.6 vs FCP-T 4.7 deliveries; 114 humans, p &lt; 0.001 vs SP, PP, BCP. E3T: Table 2 SP 65.8, PBT 66.8, FCP 71.7, MEP 89.7, E3T 114.1; training 0.5, 2.7, 7.6, 17.9, 1.9 h. GAMMA: Table 3 GAMMA-HA 91.11 / 93.09 vs MEP 76.19 and PPO+BC 85.26. GOAT: +38% and +3% in text; ~108 vs ~78 read from Fig. 4f (approximate). ZSC-Eval: Spearman 0.90 (Coordination Ring) and 1.00 (Counter Circuit) over 5 algorithms. V2: Table 2 Test-Time Simple state-augmented SP 161, XP -55, gap 230 (table); Table 1 Counter Circuit XP 59 -&gt; 140. OGC: Table 1 SoftMoE-LSTM PAIRED 13.12 vs oracle 216.76; DR 4.21, PLR 0.68, ACCEL 0.61. Others: HSP Table 2 Distant Tomato tomato-first script FCP 15.6, MEP 20.1, TrajDiv 23.3, HSP 277.9 (a script the authors wrote); PECAN 81.4% preference vs MEP (15 players); COLE mean expert-partner reward and 4 of 5 layouts best; COLE journal 0.68 to 0.88 (130 players); Behavior prior only a simulated human. Reading: metrics differ (deliveries, reward per episode, BR-prox, preference shares, return), so rows only show what each paper claimed. Limits named in the notes: simulated or small human studies, hand-set events, epsilon and weights, two-player focus, data quality for VAE-based methods (GAMMA, GOAT), and open gaps in V2 and OGC. Guest OBL (Hu et al. 2021, Hanabi Table 1): cross-play level 4 23.76 vs Other-play 21.77 (max 25; 5 seeds); not comparable with Overcooked rows and not added as a milestone (8-row cap). V2 expects OBL to do well on its Grounded Coordination layouts and to struggle on Test-Time Protocol Formation, but runs no OBL experiment.","Milestone numbers (each from the member&#x27;s own notes; not comparable across rows): Overcooked: 60 MTurk users, ANOVA F(2,224) = 6.49, PPO-BC vs SP p = .01, vs PBT p &lt; .01. FCP: Table 1 human proxy 10.6 vs FCP-T 4.7 deliveries; 114 humans, p &lt; 0.001 vs SP, PP, BCP. E3T: Table 2 SP 65.8, PBT 66.8, FCP 71.7, MEP 89.7, E3T 114.1; training 0.5, 2.7, 7.6, 17.9, 1.9 h. GAMMA: Table 3 GAMMA-HA 91.11 / 93.09 vs MEP 76.19 and PPO+BC 85.26. GOAT: +38% and +3% in text; ~108 vs ~78 read from Fig. 4f (approximate). ZSC-Eval: Spearman 0.90 (Coordination Ring) and 1.00 (Counter Circuit) over 5 algorithms. V2: Table 2 Test-Time Simple state-augmented SP 161, XP -55, gap 230 (table); Table 1 Counter Circuit XP 59 -&gt; 140. OGC: Table 1 SoftMoE-LSTM PAIRED 13.12 vs oracle 216.76; DR 4.21, PLR 0.68, ACCEL 0.61. Others: HSP Table 2 Distant Tomato tomato-first script FCP 15.6, MEP 20.1, TrajDiv 23.3, HSP 277.9 (a script the authors wrote); PECAN 81.4% preference vs MEP (15 players); COLE mean expert-partner reward and 4 of 5 layouts best; COLE journal 0.68 to 0.88 (130 players); Behavior prior only a simulated human. Reading: metrics differ (deliveries, reward per episode, BR-prox, preference shares, return), so rows only show what each paper claimed. Limits named in the notes: simulated or small human studies, hand-set events, epsilon and weights, two-player focus, data quality for VAE-based methods (GAMMA, GOAT), and open gaps in V2 and OGC. Guest OBL (Hu et al. 2021, Hanabi Table 1): cross-play level 4 23.76 vs Other-play 21.77 (max 25; 5 seeds); not comparable with Overcooked rows and not added as a milestone (8-row cap). V2 expects OBL to do well on its Grounded Coordination layouts and to struggle on Test-Time Protocol Formation, but runs no OBL experiment."]});
